    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42947" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schŏlāris</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		schola. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Of</i> or <i>belonging to a
			school</i> (late Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">incohamenta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 3, § 326</span></i>
			: murmur, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ.</span> 9, 16: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">declamatio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 36, 14</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			(Acc. to schola, I. B. 2. b.) <i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">schŏlāres</span></b> ,
				ĭum, m., <i>the imperial guard</i>, Cod. Th. 11, 18, 1; 7, 4, 34;
					<i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 12, 38, 14</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
